msgid "Part 1 — Getting Started"
msgstr "Partie 1 — Premiers pas"

msgid ""
"This part takes you from installation to a working "
":class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary`: building one, reading and "
"changing it with hierarchical keys, configuring it, and choosing between "
"the three public classes."
msgstr ""
"Cette partie vous mène de l’installation à un "
":class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary` opérationnel : le construire, le "
"lire et le modifier avec des clés hiérarchiques, le configurer, et "
"choisir entre les trois classes publiques."

msgid "Installation"
msgstr "Installation"

msgid "Install **ndict-tools** from PyPI with ``pip``:"
msgstr "Installez **ndict-tools** depuis PyPI avec ``pip`` :"

msgid "pip install ndict-tools"
msgstr "pip install ndict-tools"

msgid "or add it to a project managed by ``uv``:"
msgstr "ou ajoutez-le à un projet géré par ``uv`` :"

msgid "uv add ndict-tools"
msgstr "uv add ndict-tools"

msgid ""
"The package requires **Python 3.11 or later** and has no runtime "
"dependencies beyond the standard library."
msgstr ""
"Le paquet requiert **Python 3.11 ou une version ultérieure** et n’a "
"aucune dépendance d’exécution en dehors de la bibliothèque standard."

msgid "Building a nested dictionary"
msgstr "Construire un dictionnaire imbriqué"

msgid ""
"Pass a plain :class:`dict` to the constructor. Here is a small house of "
"one floor: each room holds its equipment, and some equipment has settings"
" of its own."
msgstr ""
"Passez un :class:`dict` simple au constructeur. Voici une petite maison "
"d’un seul étage : chaque pièce contient ses équipements, et certains "
"équipements ont leurs propres réglages."

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> house = NestedDictionary({\n"
"...     \"kitchen\": {\n"
"...         \"lights\": \"ceiling\",\n"
"...         \"heating\": {\"type\": \"radiator\", \"power\": 1500},\n"
"...     },\n"
"...     \"living room\": {\"lights\": \"floor lamp\", \"heating\": "
"{\"type\": \"fireplace\"}},\n"
"...     \"garage\": {},\n"
"...     \"garden\": {\"shed\": \"tools\"},\n"
"... })"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import NestedDictionary\n"
">>> house = NestedDictionary({\n"
"...     \"kitchen\": {\n"
"...         \"lights\": \"ceiling\",\n"
"...         \"heating\": {\"type\": \"radiator\", \"power\": 1500},\n"
"...     },\n"
"...     \"living room\": {\"lights\": \"floor lamp\", \"heating\": "
"{\"type\": \"fireplace\"}},\n"
"...     \"garage\": {},\n"
"...     \"garden\": {\"shed\": \"tools\"},\n"
"... })"

msgid ""
"The constructor converts every nested :class:`dict` into a "
":class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary`, at every level. The garage, which"
" has nothing in it yet, is an empty nested dictionary:"
msgstr ""
"Le constructeur convertit chaque :class:`dict` imbriqué en un "
":class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary`, à tous les niveaux. Le garage, "
"encore vide, est un dictionnaire imbriqué vide :"

msgid ""
">>> type(house[\"kitchen\"]).__name__\n"
"'NestedDictionary'\n"
">>> type(house[\"kitchen\"][\"heating\"]).__name__\n"
"'NestedDictionary'\n"
">>> len(house[\"garage\"])\n"
"0"
msgstr ""
">>> type(house[\"kitchen\"]).__name__\n"
"'NestedDictionary'\n"
">>> type(house[\"kitchen\"][\"heating\"]).__name__\n"
"'NestedDictionary'\n"
">>> len(house[\"garage\"])\n"
"0"

msgid ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.to_dict` gives the content back as "
"plain dictionaries, which is the easiest way to look at it:"
msgstr ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.to_dict` restitue le contenu sous "
"forme de dictionnaires simples, ce qui est le moyen le plus simple de "
"l’examiner :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> house.to_dict()[\"living room\"]\n"
"{'lights': 'floor lamp', 'heating': {'type': 'fireplace'}}"
msgstr ""
">>> house.to_dict()[\"living room\"]\n"
"{'lights': 'floor lamp', 'heating': {'type': 'fireplace'}}"

msgid ""
"The constructor accepts the same arguments as :class:`dict`: an iterable "
"of ``(key, value)`` pairs, a ``zip``, or keyword arguments. Keyword "
"arguments are data, never settings:"
msgstr ""
"Le constructeur accepte les mêmes arguments que le constructeur de "
":class:`dict` : un itérable de paires ``(key, value)``, un ``zip``, ou "
"des arguments nommés. Les arguments nommés sont toujours des données, "
"jamais des réglages :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> rooms = NestedDictionary([(\"bedroom\", {\"lights\": \"ceiling\"}), "
"(\"bathroom\", {\"lights\": \"mirror\"})])\n"
">>> rooms.to_dict()\n"
"{'bedroom': {'lights': 'ceiling'}, 'bathroom': {'lights': 'mirror'}}\n"
">>> rooms = NestedDictionary(zip([\"bedroom\", \"bathroom\"], "
"[{\"lights\": \"ceiling\"}, {\"lights\": \"mirror\"}]))\n"
">>> rooms.to_dict()\n"
"{'bedroom': {'lights': 'ceiling'}, 'bathroom': {'lights': 'mirror'}}\n"
">>> NestedDictionary(shed=\"tools\", pond={\"fish\": 3}).to_dict()\n"
"{'shed': 'tools', 'pond': {'fish': 3}}"
msgstr ""
">>> rooms = NestedDictionary([(\"bedroom\", {\"lights\": \"ceiling\"}), "
"(\"bathroom\", {\"lights\": \"mirror\"})])\n"
">>> rooms.to_dict()\n"
"{'bedroom': {'lights': 'ceiling'}, 'bathroom': {'lights': 'mirror'}}\n"
">>> rooms = NestedDictionary(zip([\"bedroom\", \"bathroom\"], "
"[{\"lights\": \"ceiling\"}, {\"lights\": \"mirror\"}]))\n"
">>> rooms.to_dict()\n"
"{'bedroom': {'lights': 'ceiling'}, 'bathroom': {'lights': 'mirror'}}\n"
">>> NestedDictionary(shed=\"tools\", pond={\"fish\": 3}).to_dict()\n"
"{'shed': 'tools', 'pond': {'fish': 3}}"

msgid ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.from_dict` builds the same structure"
" from an existing plain dictionary. It is useful when the dictionary "
"comes from elsewhere, for example a parsed configuration file:"
msgstr ""
":meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.from_dict` construit la même "
"structure à partir d’un dictionnaire simple existant. C’est utile lorsque"
" le dictionnaire vient d’ailleurs, par exemple d’un fichier de "
"configuration analysé :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> parsed = {\"cellar\": {\"lights\": \"bulb\", \"boiler\": {\"fuel\": "
"\"gas\"}}}\n"
">>> cellar = NestedDictionary.from_dict(parsed)\n"
">>> type(cellar[\"cellar\"][\"boiler\"]).__name__\n"
"'NestedDictionary'"
msgstr ""
">>> parsed = {\"cellar\": {\"lights\": \"bulb\", \"boiler\": {\"fuel\": "
"\"gas\"}}}\n"
">>> cellar = NestedDictionary.from_dict(parsed)\n"
">>> type(cellar[\"cellar\"][\"boiler\"]).__name__\n"
"'NestedDictionary'"

msgid "Hierarchical keys"
msgstr "Clés hiérarchiques"

msgid "A single key works as with a plain :class:`dict`, and keys can be chained:"
msgstr ""
"Une clé simple fonctionne comme avec un :class:`dict` simple, et les clés"
" peuvent s’enchaîner :"

msgid ""
">>> house[\"garden\"][\"shed\"]\n"
"'tools'"
msgstr ""
">>> house[\"garden\"][\"shed\"]\n"
"'tools'"

msgid ""
"A :class:`list` of keys is a *hierarchical key*: it names a path from a "
"top-level key down to a nested one, and reaches it in one step."
msgstr ""
"Une :class:`list` de clés est une *clé hiérarchique* : elle désigne un "
"chemin depuis une clé de premier niveau jusqu’à une clé imbriquée, et "
"l’atteint en une seule étape."

msgid ""
">>> house[[\"kitchen\", \"heating\", \"power\"]]\n"
"1500"
msgstr ""
">>> house[[\"kitchen\", \"heating\", \"power\"]]\n"
"1500"

msgid ""
"Writing through a hierarchical key creates the missing levels. The house "
"gets an attic, and the kitchen a new heating power:"
msgstr ""
"Écrire au moyen d’une clé hiérarchique crée les niveaux manquants. La "
"maison reçoit un grenier, et la cuisine une nouvelle puissance de "
"chauffage :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> house[[\"attic\", \"window\"]] = \"skylight\"\n"
">>> house[\"attic\"].to_dict()\n"
"{'window': 'skylight'}\n"
">>> house[[\"kitchen\", \"heating\", \"power\"]] = 2000\n"
">>> house[[\"kitchen\", \"heating\"]].to_dict()\n"
"{'type': 'radiator', 'power': 2000}"
msgstr ""
">>> house[[\"attic\", \"window\"]] = \"skylight\"\n"
">>> house[\"attic\"].to_dict()\n"
"{'window': 'skylight'}\n"
">>> house[[\"kitchen\", \"heating\", \"power\"]] = 2000\n"
">>> house[[\"kitchen\", \"heating\"]].to_dict()\n"
"{'type': 'radiator', 'power': 2000}"

msgid ""
"``del`` and :meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.pop` accept hierarchical"
" keys too. When the deleted key was the last one of its level, the "
"emptied levels above it are removed as well: taking the tools out of the "
"shed removes the garden."
msgstr ""
"``del`` et :meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.pop` acceptent aussi les "
"clés hiérarchiques. Lorsque la clé supprimée était la dernière de son "
"niveau, les niveaux vidés au-dessus d’elle sont supprimés eux aussi : "
"retirer les outils de l’abri supprime le jardin."

msgid ""
">>> del house[[\"attic\", \"window\"]]\n"
">>> \"attic\" in house\n"
"False\n"
">>> house.pop([\"garden\", \"shed\"])\n"
"'tools'\n"
">>> \"garden\" in house\n"
"False"
msgstr ""
">>> del house[[\"attic\", \"window\"]]\n"
">>> \"attic\" in house\n"
"False\n"
">>> house.pop([\"garden\", \"shed\"])\n"
"'tools'\n"
">>> \"garden\" in house\n"
"False"

msgid ""
"Only ``del`` and :meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.pop` remove levels,"
" and only the levels they empty. A level that was empty from the start, "
"like the garage, stays:"
msgstr ""
"Seuls ``del`` et :meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.pop` suppriment des"
" niveaux, et seulement ceux qu’ils vident. Un niveau vide dès le départ, "
"comme le garage, est conservé :"

msgid ""
">>> \"garage\" in house\n"
"True"
msgstr ""
">>> \"garage\" in house\n"
"True"

msgid ""
"Only a :class:`list` is read as a path. A :class:`tuple` is an ordinary "
"hashable key, as in a plain :class:`dict`:"
msgstr ""
"Seule une :class:`list` est lue comme un chemin. Un :class:`tuple` est "
"une clé hachable ordinaire, comme dans un :class:`dict` simple :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> grid = NestedDictionary({(0, 1): \"door\", 0: {1: \"window\"}})\n"
">>> grid[(0, 1)]\n"
"'door'\n"
">>> grid[[0, 1]]\n"
"'window'"
msgstr ""
">>> grid = NestedDictionary({(0, 1): \"door\", 0: {1: \"window\"}})\n"
">>> grid[(0, 1)]\n"
"'door'\n"
">>> grid[[0, 1]]\n"
"'window'"

msgid ""
"The ``in`` operator, :meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.get` and "
":meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.setdefault` take a single key, as "
"for a plain :class:`dict`. To test whether a path exists, ask the view of"
" the paths (see :doc:`paths`):"
msgstr ""
"L’opérateur ``in``, :meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.get` et "
":meth:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary.setdefault` prennent une clé simple,"
" comme pour un :class:`dict` simple. Pour tester l’existence d’un chemin,"
" interrogez la vue des chemins (voir :doc:`paths`) :"

msgid ""
">>> house.get(\"garden\", \"no garden\")\n"
"'no garden'\n"
">>> [\"kitchen\", \"heating\", \"type\"] in house.paths()\n"
"True"
msgstr ""
">>> house.get(\"garden\", \"no garden\")\n"
"'no garden'\n"
">>> [\"kitchen\", \"heating\", \"type\"] in house.paths()\n"
"True"

msgid "Configuration"
msgstr "Configuration"

msgid ""
"Every nested dictionary carries a configuration, ``default_setup``, with "
"two settings:"
msgstr ""
"Chaque dictionnaire imbriqué porte une configuration, ``default_setup``, "
"composée de deux réglages :"

msgid ""
"``indent``: the number of spaces added at each level when the dictionary "
"is printed;"
msgstr ""
"``indent`` : le nombre d’espaces ajoutés à chaque niveau lorsque le "
"dictionnaire est affiché ;"

msgid ""
"``default_factory``: what reading a missing key does. A class creates an "
"empty nested dictionary of that class under the key; ``None`` raises "
":class:`KeyError`."
msgstr ""
"``default_factory`` : l’effet de la lecture d’une clé absente. Une classe"
" crée sous la clé un dictionnaire imbriqué vide de cette classe ; "
"``None`` lève une :class:`KeyError`."

msgid ""
"Without ``default_setup``, a :class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary` uses "
"``indent`` 0 and creates :class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary` levels. "
"Pass ``default_setup`` to choose; it needs both settings. Reading it "
"returns the settings as an ordered list of pairs:"
msgstr ""
"Sans ``default_setup``, un :class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary` utilise"
" 0 pour ``indent`` et crée des niveaux "
":class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary`. Passez ``default_setup`` pour "
"choisir ; les deux réglages sont alors obligatoires. Sa lecture renvoie "
"les réglages sous forme de liste ordonnée de paires :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> kitchen = NestedDictionary(\n"
"...     {\"lights\": \"ceiling\", \"heating\": {\"type\": \"radiator\", "
"\"power\": 1500}},\n"
"...     default_setup={\"indent\": 2, \"default_factory\": "
"NestedDictionary},\n"
"... )\n"
">>> kitchen.default_setup\n"
"[('indent', 2), ('default_factory', <class "
"'ndict_tools.core.NestedDictionary'>)]"
msgstr ""
">>> kitchen = NestedDictionary(\n"
"...     {\"lights\": \"ceiling\", \"heating\": {\"type\": \"radiator\", "
"\"power\": 1500}},\n"
"...     default_setup={\"indent\": 2, \"default_factory\": "
"NestedDictionary},\n"
"... )\n"
">>> kitchen.default_setup\n"
"[('indent', 2), ('default_factory', <class "
"'ndict_tools.core.NestedDictionary'>)]"

msgid ""
"The list is the normalized form of the configuration: always the same "
"order, whatever the form it was given in. Printing uses ``indent``:"
msgstr ""
"Cette liste est la forme normalisée de la configuration : toujours dans "
"le même ordre, quelle que soit la forme sous laquelle elle a été donnée. "
"L’affichage utilise ``indent`` :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> print(kitchen)\n"
"{\n"
"  lights : ceiling,\n"
"  heating : {\n"
"      type : radiator,\n"
"      power : 1500,\n"
"  },\n"
"}"
msgstr ""
">>> print(kitchen)\n"
"{\n"
"  lights : ceiling,\n"
"  heating : {\n"
"      type : radiator,\n"
"      power : 1500,\n"
"  },\n"
"}"

msgid ""
"All levels of a nested dictionary share its configuration. Assigning "
"``default_setup`` changes it at every level:"
msgstr ""
"Tous les niveaux d’un dictionnaire imbriqué partagent sa configuration. "
"Affecter ``default_setup`` la modifie à tous les niveaux :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> kitchen.default_setup = {\"indent\": 4, \"default_factory\": None}\n"
">>> kitchen[\"heating\"].default_setup\n"
"[('indent', 4), ('default_factory', None)]"
msgstr ""
">>> kitchen.default_setup = {\"indent\": 4, \"default_factory\": None}\n"
">>> kitchen[\"heating\"].default_setup\n"
"[('indent', 4), ('default_factory', None)]"

msgid "Choosing a class"
msgstr "Choisir une classe"

msgid ""
"The three public classes have the same interface. They differ in what "
"reading a missing key does, that is, in their ``default_factory``:"
msgstr ""
"Les trois classes publiques ont la même interface. Elles diffèrent par "
"l’effet de la lecture d’une clé absente, c’est-à-dire par leur réglage "
"``default_factory`` :"

msgid "Class"
msgstr "Classe"

msgid "Reading a missing key"
msgstr "Lecture d’une clé absente"

msgid ":class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary`"
msgstr ":class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary`"

msgid ""
"Creates an empty nested dictionary under the key, like "
":class:`collections.defaultdict`. The ``default_factory`` can be changed "
"in ``default_setup``."
msgstr ""
"Crée un dictionnaire imbriqué vide sous la clé, comme un "
":class:`collections.defaultdict`. Le réglage ``default_factory`` peut "
"être modifié dans ``default_setup``."

msgid ":class:`~ndict_tools.StrictNestedDictionary`"
msgstr ":class:`~ndict_tools.StrictNestedDictionary`"

msgid "Raises :class:`KeyError`. The ``default_factory`` is always ``None``."
msgstr ""
"Lève une :class:`KeyError`. Le réglage ``default_factory`` vaut toujours "
"``None``."

msgid ":class:`~ndict_tools.SmoothNestedDictionary`"
msgstr ":class:`~ndict_tools.SmoothNestedDictionary`"

msgid ""
"Creates an empty :class:`~ndict_tools.SmoothNestedDictionary` under the "
"key. The ``default_factory`` is always "
":class:`~ndict_tools.SmoothNestedDictionary`."
msgstr ""
"Crée un :class:`~ndict_tools.SmoothNestedDictionary` vide sous la clé. Le"
" réglage ``default_factory`` vaut toujours "
":class:`~ndict_tools.SmoothNestedDictionary`."

msgid ""
"With a :class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary`, reading a room that does "
"not exist adds it:"
msgstr ""
"Avec un :class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary`, lire une pièce qui "
"n’existe pas l’ajoute :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> plan = NestedDictionary({\"kitchen\": {\"lights\": \"ceiling\"}})\n"
">>> plan[\"office\"].to_dict()\n"
"{}\n"
">>> \"office\" in plan\n"
"True"
msgstr ""
">>> plan = NestedDictionary({\"kitchen\": {\"lights\": \"ceiling\"}})\n"
">>> plan[\"office\"].to_dict()\n"
"{}\n"
">>> \"office\" in plan\n"
"True"

msgid ""
"This suits a house you are still furnishing. To check an inventory that "
"is already complete, a :class:`~ndict_tools.StrictNestedDictionary` "
"reports the unknown room instead:"
msgstr ""
"Cela convient à une maison que vous êtes encore en train de meubler. Pour"
" vérifier un inventaire déjà complet, un "
":class:`~ndict_tools.StrictNestedDictionary` signale au contraire la "
"pièce inconnue :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import StrictNestedDictionary\n"
">>> inventory = StrictNestedDictionary({\"kitchen\": {\"lights\": "
"\"ceiling\"}})\n"
">>> inventory[\"office\"]\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"    ...\n"
"KeyError: 'office'"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import StrictNestedDictionary\n"
">>> inventory = StrictNestedDictionary({\"kitchen\": {\"lights\": "
"\"ceiling\"}})\n"
">>> inventory[\"office\"]\n"
"Traceback (most recent call last):\n"
"    ...\n"
"KeyError: 'office'"

msgid ""
":class:`~ndict_tools.StrictNestedDictionary` and "
":class:`~ndict_tools.SmoothNestedDictionary` keep their "
"``default_factory`` whatever ``default_setup`` says. Only ``indent`` can "
"be chosen:"
msgstr ""
":class:`~ndict_tools.StrictNestedDictionary` et "
":class:`~ndict_tools.SmoothNestedDictionary` conservent leur réglage "
"``default_factory`` quoi que dise ``default_setup``. Seul le réglage "
"``indent`` peut être choisi :"

#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
">>> from ndict_tools import SmoothNestedDictionary\n"
">>> sketch = SmoothNestedDictionary(default_setup={\"indent\": 2, "
"\"default_factory\": None})\n"
">>> sketch.default_setup\n"
"[('indent', 2), ('default_factory', <class "
"'ndict_tools.core.SmoothNestedDictionary'>)]\n"
">>> type(sketch[\"attic\"][\"window\"]).__name__\n"
"'SmoothNestedDictionary'"
msgstr ""
">>> from ndict_tools import SmoothNestedDictionary\n"
">>> sketch = SmoothNestedDictionary(default_setup={\"indent\": 2, "
"\"default_factory\": None})\n"
">>> sketch.default_setup\n"
"[('indent', 2), ('default_factory', <class "
"'ndict_tools.core.SmoothNestedDictionary'>)]\n"
">>> type(sketch[\"attic\"][\"window\"]).__name__\n"
"'SmoothNestedDictionary'"

msgid ""
"Because reading a missing key adds it, a tool that reads keys it does not"
" know changes the data. The variable viewers of debuggers built on "
"``pydevd``, such as those of PyCharm and VS Code, read the attributes of "
"a dictionary subclass as keys first: inspecting a "
":class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary` can add keys such as "
"``default_setup`` or ``_default_setup``. To inspect without side effects,"
" use a :class:`~ndict_tools.StrictNestedDictionary` or set "
"``default_factory`` to ``None``."
msgstr ""
"Comme la lecture d’une clé absente l’ajoute, un outil qui lit des clés "
"qu’il ne connaît pas modifie les données. Les inspecteurs de variables "
"des débogueurs fondés sur ``pydevd``, comme ceux de PyCharm et de VS "
"Code, lisent d’abord comme des clés les attributs d’une sous-classe de "
"dictionnaire : inspecter un :class:`~ndict_tools.NestedDictionary` peut "
"ajouter des clés telles que ``default_setup`` ou ``_default_setup``. Pour"
" inspecter sans effet de bord, utilisez un "
":class:`~ndict_tools.StrictNestedDictionary` ou réglez "
"``default_factory`` sur ``None``."

msgid ""
"Keep in mind the difference between the attribute "
"``house.default_setup``, the configuration, and the item "
"``house[\"default_setup\"]``, a key of the data."
msgstr ""
"Gardez à l’esprit la différence entre l’attribut ``house.default_setup``,"
" la configuration, et l’élément ``house[\"default_setup\"]``, une clé des"
" données."

msgid "Where to go next"
msgstr "Pour aller plus loin"

msgid ""
":doc:`exploring` searches, walks through, measures, compares and copies a"
" whole nested dictionary."
msgstr ""
":doc:`exploring` recherche, parcourt, mesure, compare et copie un "
"dictionnaire imbriqué entier."

msgid ":doc:`paths` lists, filters and compares the paths of a nested dictionary."
msgstr ""
":doc:`paths` énumère, filtre et compare les chemins d’un dictionnaire "
"imbriqué."

msgid ":doc:`serialization` saves a nested dictionary to JSON or pickle."
msgstr ""
":doc:`serialization` enregistre un dictionnaire imbriqué en JSON ou avec "
"pickle."

msgid ":doc:`extending` explains how to write your own subclass."
msgstr ":doc:`extending` explique comment écrire votre propre sous-classe."

